      "detail": "Opener: Tue 9/29 vs. Canadiens",
      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "A team can feel its way toward October without winning anything that counts, and Toronto is there now - sorting the last cuts, the line combinations, the goaltending pecking order, all of it under the cold light of a season opener four days away. <strong>The most telling moment came in Arizona, where the Maple Leafs visited the Mayich family in hospital before practice and then skated in shirts and hats honoring Matthew Mayich.</strong> That kind of gesture tells you the room still has a pulse. The scoreboard says little in preseason, though the Leafs did beat Ottawa 6-1 on Sep. 23 and finished these exhibitions with some swagger after the earlier split with Montreal. The real question is whether the new goaltending setup is sturdier than last year's wobble. <strong>Tuesday's opener against Montreal will show whether this camp was polish - or just noise.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated September 27, 2026"
      },
