        "body": "A new season begins with a familiar burden in Toronto - hope, heat, and a roster still trying to prove it fits. <strong>Kawhi Leonard is back in the conversation and Bobby Webster is setting a high bar</strong>, which is exactly what a camp on the edge should sound like. The Raptors arrive at training camp with the kind of decisions that matter: who claims the wing minutes, how RJ Barrett and Jakob Poeltl are slotted, and which young legs can survive the grind. They do not open the regular season until Oct. 21 against Chicago, so this stretch is about sorting the board, not chasing headlines. <strong>Saturday's preseason opener against Miami will be the first real test of the pecking order</strong> - and the first chance to see whether this group has backbone or just promises.",
